 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the provision of\ninformation relating to renewable energy technologies and programs",
    "basePrintNo": "S8717",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8717-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 39,
       "fullName": "Robert Rolison",
       "imgName": "1336_Robert_Rolison.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1519,
       "sessionMemberId": 2356,
       "sessionYear": 2025,
       "shortName": "ROLISON"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1912, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8717\n\nSPONSOR: HINCHEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to the provision\nof information relating to renewable energy technologies and programs\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo direct NYSERDA to use every available method to inform the public\nabout the programs they operate that could save consumers money on their\nenergy costs or help them lower their energy use,\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one directs NYSERDA to specifically include information on what\nincentives, affordability programs and energy efficiency programs are\navailable in its education and outreach efforts. It also directs the\nauthority to conduct outreach via television, radio, social media, print\nadvertising, with libraries and other public institutions and to recruit\npeople to serve as public ambassadors.\n\nSection two states the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNYSERDA is responsible for a host of programs and incentives to assist\nconsumers with growing energy costs and find green solutions to reduce\ntheir energy use. While these programs can be a great success for those\nwho take advantage of them, we have seen that educating consumers on\nwhat programs exist and how to access them can be a significant barrier.\n\nThis bill will help increase the visibility of existing NYSERDA programs\nby giving them specific directions on how to conduct their education and\noutreach. This legislation will require NYSERDA to educate consumers on\nwhat incentives, affordability programs and energy efficiency programs\nalready exist and it directs them to use television, radio, social media\nand print advertising, work with libraries and other public institutions\nand to recruit people to serve as public ambassadors. Increasing partic-\nipation in these programs is extremely important for helping consumers\nlower their energy costs and help the state reach its CLCPA goals. This\nbill will require NYSERDA to use every available avenue to increase\npublic awareness of what programs exist.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\namendments to subdivision 1 of section 1912 of the public authorities\nlaw made by section one of this act shall not affect the repeal of such\nsection and shall be deemed repealed therewith.\n",
